<div class="manual-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">BUZNET CRM · USER GUIDE</span><h1>Help & user manual</h1><p>Search the guide or browse the main workflows below.</p></div><input id="manual-search" class="manual-search" type="search" placeholder="Search help topics…" aria-label="Search help topics"></div>
<div class="manual-grid" id="manual-grid">
<article class="manual-card"><h2>Getting started</h2><ol><li>Sign in with your Owner or Manager account.</li><li>Set the business name and currency under Settings.</li><li>Add customers and products or services before creating invoices.</li><li>Use the dashboard to review recorded activity. Empty values mean records have not been entered yet.</li></ol><div class="manual-note">The current workspace is stored in your MySQL database. Keep your XAMPP MySQL service running while using the app.</div></article>
<article class="manual-card"><h2>Customers and leads</h2><ul><li><a href="customers.php">Customers</a>: add, search, edit, archive and view invoice history.</li><li><a href="leads.php">Leads</a>: create a lead, then move its stage using the dropdown.</li><li>Mark a lead Won to show the Convert to customer action.</li><li>Lead conversion checks matching email or phone. Link an existing customer when one is found.</li><li>Archiving a customer hides it from new work but retains linked financial records.</li></ul></article>
<article class="manual-card"><h2>Quotations and invoices</h2><ul><li><a href="quotations.php">Quotations</a>: create an estimate, set its validity, then mark it Sent, Accepted or Rejected.</li><li>Accepted quotations can be converted in workspaces that are not GST-registered. For regular GST registration, create the invoice from the catalog so HSN/SAC and tax split are verified at issue time.</li><li><a href="invoices.php">Invoices</a>: prices and tax rates are re-read from the catalog on the server when issued.</li><li>Open an invoice and select Download PDF for a saved PDF, or Print to use the browser print dialog.</li><li>Issued invoices retain customer and business snapshots. Unpaid issued invoices can be voided from their detail page.</li></ul></article>
<article class="manual-card"><h2>Payments and expenses</h2><ul><li><a href="payments.php">Payments</a>: record a receipt against an open invoice. The balance is recalculated automatically.</li><li>Payment reversals are Owner-only and require a reason. A reversal is retained in history.</li><li><a href="expenses.php">Expenses</a>: enter date, category, description and amount to include the record in reports.</li><li>The app records business cash activity; it is not a complete double-entry accounting ledger.</li></ul></article>
<article class="manual-card"><h2>Managers and access</h2><ul><li>Owners create and disable Manager accounts under <a href="managers.php">Managers</a>.</li><li>Grant module view and edit access separately. Edit access is ignored unless view access is also granted.</li><li>Access is enforced by server-side checks on supported routes and writes.</li><li>Managers cannot change the business profile or download the Owner backup.</li></ul></article>
<article class="manual-card"><h2>Reports and backup</h2><ul><li><a href="reports.php">Reports</a> supports a date range and a customer summary CSV export.</li><li>Owners can download a business JSON snapshot from <a href="settings.php#backup">Settings → Backup</a>.</li><li>The export excludes password hashes. Store it somewhere private and encrypted.</li><li>Restore is under Settings → Restore Backup: upload and preview a backup from the same workspace, then enter your current Owner password and type RESTORE. Restore saves a private pre-restore recovery copy first.</li></ul></article>
<article class="manual-card"><h2>Setup and troubleshooting</h2><ul><li>Start Apache and MySQL in XAMPP to serve the local app.</li><li>If the database connection fails, confirm database `buznet_crm` and the `BUZNET_DB_*` PHP environment settings.</li><li>For a new database, import <code>database/schema.sql</code>.</li><li>For an existing database, apply only missing migration scripts in sequence. Migrations 005 and 006 are applied in this workspace.</li><li>Installation details are in <a href="docs/installation.md">the installation guide</a>.</li></ul></article>
<article class="manual-card"><h2>GST invoice setup and limits</h2><ul><li>The Owner sets legal supplier name, address, GST registration and state in Settings. Set each item HSN/SAC and configured GST rate in Products, and customer GSTIN/address/state in Customers.</li><li>Regular GST invoice tax is split into CGST+SGST for a matching supplier/place-of-supply state code, otherwise IGST. New invoices use a consecutive financial-year number series. Composition and unregistered profiles issue non-taxed documents.</li><li>GST portal lookup, return filing, reverse charge, credit/debit notes, e-invoice/IRN, e-way bills and special place-of-supply determinations are not implemented. Verify rates and treatment with a tax professional.</li><li>Password recovery uses PHP mail. Configure XAMPP Sendmail or SMTP before expecting reset emails.</li></ul></article><article class="manual-card"><h2>Known feature gaps</h2><ul><li>AI assistant and provider setup are not implemented.</li><li>Demo data/reset and advanced GST compliance workflows are not implemented.</li></ul></article>
